	<text xml:lang="en">
		<body>
<div><head n="1" coords="1,70.87,633.10,82.81,10.75">Introduction</head><p coords="1,70.87,655.53,220.08,9.46"><s coords="1,70.87,655.53,220.08,9.46">Large LMs based on the Transformer architecture have become the central building block of many NLP applications.</s></p></div>
<div><head coords="2,70.87,100.00,100.00,9.81">A closer look.</head><p coords="2,70.87,110.00,220.08,9.46"><s coords="2,70.87,110.00,220.08,9.46">Previous work using the TransInner method freezes the Transformer body.</s></p></div>
<div><head n="2" coords="9,306.14,73.58,75.07,10.75">Conclusion</head><p coords="9,305.63,95.35,218.78,9.46"><s coords="9,305.63,95.35,218.78,9.46">We introduced WECHSEL, a method to transfer monolingual language models to new languages.</s></p></div>
<div><head coords="9,306.14,388.66,111.46,10.75">Acknowledgments</head><p coords="9,306.14,410.43,218.27,9.46"><s coords="9,306.14,410.43,218.27,9.46">Research supported with Cloud TPUs from Google's TPU Research Cloud (TRC).</s></p></div>
<div><p coords="9,306.14,423.97,218.54,9.46"><s coords="9,306.14,423.97,218.54,9.46">We thank Andy Koh and Artus Krohn-Grimberghe for providing additional computational resources.</s></p></div>
<div><head coords="12,306.14,442.14,146.27,10.75">A Grid search over k and τ</head><p coords="12,305.80,467.14,218.61,9.81"><s coords="12,305.80,467.14,218.61,9.81">To choose number of neighbors k and temperature τ for WECHSEL we conduct a grid search over linear probes (Figure <ref type="figure">5</ref>).</s></p></div>
<div><head coords="12,306.14,600.00,146.27,10.75">A.1 Probing tasks</head><p coords="12,305.80,620.00,218.61,9.81"><s coords="12,305.80,620.00,218.61,9.81">We probe on NLI by taking a concatenation of the mean of all token representations in the premise and the hypothesis.</s></p></div>
<div><head coords="12,306.14,650.00,50.00,9.81">Summary.</head><p coords="12,305.80,660.00,218.61,9.81"><s coords="12,305.80,660.00,218.61,9.81">The grid search picks k and τ for all languages at once.</s></p></div>
<div><head coords="12,306.14,697.93,110.78,10.75">B Hyperparameters</head><p coords="12,306.14,723.27,218.27,9.46"><s coords="12,306.14,723.27,218.27,9.46">Hyperparameters used to fine-tune RoBERTa on downstream tasks are shown in Table 6.</s></p></div>
<div><head coords="13,306.14,100.00,110.78,10.75">C. Qualitative subword correspondence</head><p coords="13,70.35,463.89,218.78,9.46"><s coords="13,70.35,463.89,218.78,9.46">Samples of tokens in each language and their most similar tokens are shown in Table 8.</s></p></div>
